 "transcriber_notes": "SnowPilot chart (FPDF export, 994x840 raster). Height axis in the middle, 3.16 px/cm; boundaries 164, 154, 138, 128, 111, 82, 45 (+-0.3 cm; table lines and bar edges agree). Hardness bars grow leftward on a non-uniform axis (ticks F 435, 4F 399, 1F 351, P 255, K 111, I 63 px, with third-class minor ticks at 427/411, 387/366, 329/285, 223/149 px), read against the ticks: 164-154 cm on the P- tick, 138-128 cm on the 1F+ tick; the 82-45 cm bar slants from P to the P+ tick. Temperatures from the red dots on the top axis (-11 to 0 degC, ticks every degree, about 38.7 px per degree, 0 at the height axis), read between neighbouring ticks; the 178 and 170 cm dots lie on the SnowPilot logo (centres read by eye, +-0.1 degC) and the 0 cm dot on the frame. Densities printed at the top of each table row. The CTN arrow points at the ground (height null)."
